NVM devices are increasingly being used to enhance the capacity of the total available memory. We need to bear in mind that nonvolatile memory devices are in terms of performance between hard disks and regular DRAM memory. The latency of a hard disk is in milliseconds, whereas the latency of nonvolatile memory is typically in microseconds or in the 100s of nanoseconds range. The DRAM memory on the other hand has a sub 100-ns latency. The advantage of nonvolatile memories 
_<u>⃝</u>_ c Smruti R. Sarangi 
